    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as the clear engine of the offense. With an elite score of 83.29, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a high-run-environment park factor (+16%) and a favorable matchup against Littell, whose 4.82 xERA provides the ideal ceiling for **Gunnar Henderson** to capitalize on his dynamic platoon advantage. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (70.58) and **Josh Jung** (67.50) are high-priority starts; despite the presence of Bradish on the mound, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**\u2019s 16% park boost significantly inflates his floor, while **Josh Jung** finds himself in a prime spot to exploit Bieber\u2019s 5.04 xERA. We are also leaning heavily on the power-speed upside of **Josh Lowe** (68.96), whose score remains high despite a penalty for facing an elite defensive catcher, as the matchup against Civale offers significant run-production potential.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was keeping **Coby Mayo** (61.64) on the bench. While **Coby Mayo** benefits from the same park factors that lift **Gunnar Henderson**, his projected efficiency was marginally lower than that of **Wade Meckler** and **Kyle Tucker**, forcing a conservative approach to preserve our games-played caps. While **Kyle Tucker** (64.46) is currently batting 7th, his base talent and situational splits against King remain superior to the alternatives on the bench. We are tracking **Andy Pages** (61.30) closely; while he is a solid start, his score is slightly suppressed by a -2% penalty for facing an elite hold pitcher capable of shutting down the running game, a critical consideration given our strategic emphasis on SB efficiency. No major weather risks are flagged, but we are monitoring the lineup status of **Wade Meckler**, whose score of 57.26 is highly dependent on his platoon advantage against Civale.",
